  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "note-oilslick",
      "x": -520,
      "y": -160,
      "w": 360,
      "text": "OILSLICK (TYPE \u221e) — the chosen Y2K direction, fully working: boot splash, 9 screens (KITS/KIT/TAPE/CHOP/PLAY/SYNTH/EXPORT/\u2699/HELP), WebAudio pads + THUMP, capture bubble, scheme picker. Tokens + Android notes in HANDOFF.md."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-direction",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -160,
      "w": 360,
      "text": "Direction: 90s desktop quirk x cassette tape.\nGray bevels = tool chrome. Dark green LCD = anything that plays or shows sound.\nThe ring buffer IS the tape - the metaphor is the mental model, not a costume."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-trim",
      "x": 450,
      "y": -110,
      "w": 300,
      "text": "Trim = tape under a fixed needle: you drag the AUDIO, the playhead never moves. Precision without tiny handles."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-bubble",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1400,
      "w": 300,
      "text": "During capture the bubble IS the app. One tap = snip, never opens a screen. Trim always happens later."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-schemes",
      "x": 1880,
      "y": 900,
      "w": 320,
      "text": "Schemes = swapped tokens, nothing else. Class colors are fixed in every scheme - pad color is the shared language with the MPC. The Main artboard has a live Scheme tweak: flip it from the chip above the frame."
    }
  ],
  "launch": {
    "view": "canvas"
  }
}